Qt for Python 6.12.1 is a bug-fix release.

For more details, refer to the online documentation included in this
distribution. The documentation is also available online:

https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython/

Some of the changes listed in this file include issue tracking numbers
corresponding to tasks in the Qt Bug Tracker:

https://bugreports.qt.io/

Each of these identifiers can be entered in the bug tracker to obtain more
information about a particular change.

****************************************************************************
*                                  PySide6                                 *
****************************************************************************

 - [PYSIDE-768]  QtAsyncio: Futures and tasks now follow asyncio more closely
                 (callback contexts, per-task contexts, cancellation state),
                 fixing failures with anyio-based libraries such as
                 Pydantic AI.
 - [PYSIDE-1112] Documentation: examples have been updated and their
                 documentation has been improved.
 - [PYSIDE-2352] iOS: QtQmlFeatures has been added.
 - [PYSIDE-3366] SBOM support has been added. The build can now produce SBOM
                 data when passing option --sbom.
 - [PYSIDE-3398] iOS: The minimum Python version has been raised to 3.15.
 - [PYSIDE-3471] PySide lazy imports have been fixed to handle
                 Python 3.15 lazy imports.
 - [PYSIDE-3472] type hints: PEP 526 annotations are now used for class
                 attributes.
 - [PYSIDE-3475] Missing libraries required for QtGraphs2D have been added.
 - [PYSIDE-3478] Workarounds for lock-ups occurring with QMediaPlayer and
                 signal/slot connections have been added.
 - [PYSIDE-3479] Double deletion of widgets in certain layout setups
                 has been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3480] Documentation: Broken JIRA links in the changelog have
                 been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3488] Android Deployment: Qt libraries are now loaded in
                 dependency order, fixing an issue with Qt Quick Controls.
 - [PYSIDE-3489] A memory leak related to QTreeWidgetItem::takeChild(ren)
                 has been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3490] iOS: Third party packages are now supported.
 - [PYSIDE-3500] A crash accessing header items of QStandardItemModel
                 has been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3501] Android: pyside6-android-deploy now falls back to
                 existing library names.
 - [PYSIDE-3505] metaobjectdump: A crash caused by lambdas in a property
                 getter has been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3511] A deadlock occurring when using QImageReader with
                 multiple threads has been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3512] Deadlocks occurring when using QAction as a default
                 action of a QToolButton with multiple threads have been
                 fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3513] A deadlock occurring when instantiating a QMediaPlayer
                 with multiple threads has been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3514] A deadlock occurring when instantiating QAudioOutput
                 with multiple threads has been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3515] A few incorrect parent-child relationships added by the
                 generator heuristics for a number of QtWidgets accessors
                 have been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3516] CMake build: Some missing .pyi files are now installed.
 - [PYSIDE-3517] A crash occurring in Python 3.15 when passing a temporary
                 to QTimer.singleShot has been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3518] Bindings for QTextDocument's resource provider have
                 been added.
 - [PYSIDE-3521] A crash using QTreeWidgetItemIterator has been fixed.

****************************************************************************
*                                  Shiboken6                               *
****************************************************************************

 - [PYSIDE-3221] Python 3.15 is now supported.
 - [PYSIDE-3424] Crashes due to decreasing the refcount of Py_None to 0 and
                 below when running against Python 3.10/3.11 have been
                 addressed by raising the minimum build version for
                 Limited API to Python 3.13.5. This version contains a
                 fix for the issue (see GH 134989).
 - [PYSIDE-3504] The required libxml dependency of shiboken6_generator has
                 been raised to version 2.15.2, past the LibXml2 SONAME-Bump
                 from libxml2.so.2 → libxml2.so.16. Documentation-generator
                 features based on libxslt (XSLT-based modifications and
                 doxygen support) are for now disabled in the wheels.
                 Using them requires building shiboken6_generator.
 - [PYSIDE-3473] libshiboken: A bug causing the delete-in-main-thread
                 attribute to have no effect for Python-derived classes
                 has been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3507] Due to a change in CPython 3.15, negative flag values will
                 now be converted to their unsigned equivalents
                 (see GH-107538/PR132273). In 6.13, this will be the case
                 for older Python versions, too.
 - [PYSIDE-3515] Generator return value heuristics will no longer set
                 a parent on a return value in case it already has one.
 - [PYSIDE-3525] Generator return value heuristics now check for
                 reference cycles.
